# Follow-up to 2026-10-03-8.play / 2026-10-03-8-idle.play: the daily's own
# win screen showed a "25-MAN HEROIC" advance button and a "next: The
# Bonegrinder - 25 player heroic" banner on a FRESH save whose only real
# unlock should be Bonegrinder 10-normal. Reading src/progress.ts's chain
# (Bonegrinder 10N -> 10H -> 25N -> 25H -> ...) and src/main.ts's advanceTier
# (1511-1528) against updateDaily's start handler (1782-1787, which sets
# `encounter`/`difficulty`/`party` straight off the daily, not off the real
# chain) suggests the daily's own fixed 25-player setting feeds `setting()`
# the same as an ordinary pull would, so clearing it and tapping NEXT would
# set `unlocked` to the 25-heroic rung -- skipping 10-heroic and 25-normal,
# neither of which this fresh save has ever actually cleared in a real raid.
# This checks what pressing the button actually does, not just what the code
# says it should.
open
tap daily
tap class:13
tap start
waitscreen fight 15
play idle 200
state
shot daily-kill
targets
tap outcome:next
waitscreen fight 10
shot after-next
state
key escape
shot post-escape
targets
tap raid
shot raid-screen
targets
